> planner/tools/openai_web_search.py
> """
> """
> OpenAI Responses API web-search tool adapter.
> 
> This module implements the normalized ``ToolCallable`` protocol for OpenAI's
> ``web_search`` Responses API tool. It accepts a ``ToolInvocation``, validates
> per-invocation configuration, performs a web search, and returns structured
> ``ToolResult``/``Artifact`` objects rather than treating provider-generated text
> as trusted prompt content.
> 
> Usage::
> 
>     from openai import OpenAI
>     from tools.openai_web_search import (
>         OpenAIWebSearchSettings,
>         build_openai_web_search_tool,
>     )
> 
>     tool = build_openai_web_search_tool(
>         OpenAI(),
>         defaults=OpenAIWebSearchSettings(
>             model="gpt-6-luna",
>             search_context_size="high",
>             external_web_access=True,
>         ),
>         # Optional operator policy: callers cannot widen this allow-list.
>         hard_allowed_domains=["www.who.int", "www.cdc.gov"],
>     )
> 
>     invocation = ToolInvocation(
>         operation_id="op-123",
>         conversation_id="conversation-456",
>         arguments={"query": "Latest WHO guidance on heat-health action plans"},
>         config={
>             "search_context_size": "high",
>             "user_location": {
>                 "type": "approximate",
>                 "country": "CA",
>                 "city": "Toronto",
>                 "region": "Ontario",
>                 "timezone": "America/Toronto",
>             },
>         },
>         context=None,
>         provenance_requirements={},
>     )
> 
>     result = tool.fn(invocation)
> 
> ``result`` contains a structured search-response artifact, one artifact per
> consulted source, and optionally the raw provider response. Search answers,
> snippets, source metadata, and raw results are untrusted external material:
> callers should persist, inspect, cite, and selectively summarize them, but must
> never inject them blindly into system instructions.
> 
> Supported invocation ``config`` keys include ``model``,
> ``search_context_size``, ``allowed_domains``, ``blocked_domains``,
> ``user_location``, ``external_web_access``, ``return_token_budget``,
> ``search_content_types``, ``image_max_results``, ``image_caption``,
> ``force_search``, and ``include_raw_results``. Domain lists contain bare
> hostnames and are limited to 100 entries by the OpenAI API.
> """
> 
