> Mostly: **put the evidence-brief logic in `JavaScriptPlanningResponder._synthesis_messages()` once**. Both `WebRagJavaScriptResponder` and `ParallelDirectWebJavaScriptResponder` inherit that method and already route through it.
> 
> ## What is already covered
> 
> ### `WebRagJavaScriptResponder`
> 
> Its `chat_response()` does:
> 
> ```python
> enriched = self._context_with_search(...)
> return super().chat_response(plan, enriched, ...)
> ```
> 
> `super()` is `JavaScriptPlanningResponder.chat_response()`, which eventually calls:
> 
> ```python
> self._synthesis_messages(...)
> ```
> 
> So your new `_execution_evidence_for_llm()` logic applies automatically.
> 
> ### `ParallelDirectWebJavaScriptResponder`
> 
> Its `chat_response()` does:
> 
> ```python
> phase_two = self._phase_two_context(...)
> return JavaScriptPlanningResponder.chat_response(self, plan, phase_two, ...)
> ```
> 
> and streaming calls `JavaScriptPlanningResponder.stream_response(...)`, which calls:
> 
> ```python
> context2 = self._phase_two_context(...)
> ...
> self._synthesis_messages(plan, context2, ...)
> ```
> 
> So it is also covered automatically.
> 
